  "reviewed_behaviors": [
    "Both public storage entry methods validate finite offsets, relative height and mass before indexing.",
    "Non-finite float increments are rejected before accessing the destination. Prospective totals are checked and assigned under the original leaf-array lock.",
    "Finite signed masses, signed zero and subnormal contributions retain baseline behavior. This patch deliberately does not impose a new nonnegative-mass policy.",
    "A rejected call leaves every destination cell unchanged and increments the long counter once. Valid writes in another source group remain usable.",
    "Already non-finite cells remain non-finite; the guard rejects additions to them without replacing or repairing their contents.",
    "The counter is drained after both blocking tracking drivers complete, once per completed weather situation. Cancellation exits before that normal completion report.",
    "Finite invalid indices, malformed grid geometry and other concentration/deposition/receptor sums remain outside this change."
  ],
